  },
  "pca": {
    "method": "centered (NOT unit-variance-scaled) SVD PCA on log1p-CPM matrix over all 250 genes; top 15 PCs retained",
    "details": "self-implemented SVD projection",
    "justification": "log1p already places genes on a comparable scale. Empirically on this dataset, unit-variance z-scoring inflated noise PCs (PC1 only 1.8% var; 82 PCs for 80% var) and unstable clustering, whereas un-scaled log-PCA gives PC1 = 19.2% var and a stable partition. HVG (top 50% by CV) was evaluated and produced an imbalanced 1+3 partition with negative silhouette; all-gene PCA produced the better-balanced, better separated 2+2 partition."
  },
  "clustering": {
    "method": "Lloyd k-means on the PCA embedding (best of 40 fixed-seed restarts RNG(42)); k = metadata n_clusters (4)",
